        <definition>typedef void(* dxl2_packet_handler_t) (const struct dxl2_packet *packet, void *context)</definition>
        <argsstring>)(const struct dxl2_packet *packet, void *context)</argsstring>
        <name>dxl2_packet_handler_t</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Handle one valid packet received by the link. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The packet pointer is valid only for the duration of the callback. Copy any data that must be retained after the callback returns. The handler may call <ref refid="group__dxl2__link_1gaaf14e858ba2e54e6a63fda49b87660bb" kindref="member">dxl2_link_send</ref> on the same link to answer.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>packet</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Decoded packet with byte stuffing removed. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>context</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Value of <ref refid="structdxl2__link__config_1ae3157684d15e304afc72919ef0073681" kindref="member">dxl2_link_config::handler_context</ref>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
